// Expected: u1.
//
// The second token is a hash of the first, and both are on the wire. The
// attacker hashes tok0 and compares the result with tok1: in the world where
// the two tokens come from one chain the comparison succeeds, in the world
// where tok1 belongs to another chain it fails, so the tokens are linked.
//
// The shared-secret witness used to withhold each observed value from the
// attacker and look for a common origin among what remained, so a token that
// is itself the origin of the other was never found: tok0 has no origin the
// attacker holds, and the search stopped there. A queried value that appears
// among the origins of the other queried value is now a witness in its own
// right. unlink_chain_forward.vp is the counterweight, where neither token
// can be recomputed from the other.

attacker[passive]

principal Alice[
	generates sk0
	tok0 = HASH(sk0)
	tok1 = HASH(tok0)
]

Alice -> Bob: tok0, tok1

principal Bob[
	_ = HASH(tok0)
	_ = HASH(tok1)
]

queries[
	unlinkability? tok0, tok1
]
